---
import ToolPage from '../../../components/ToolPage.astro';
import { toolById } from '../../../seo/tool-registry';
const definition = toolById('measure-my-car');
---
<ToolPage {definition} alternates={[{ hreflang: 'en', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/tools/measure-my-car/' }, { hreflang: 'de', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/de/tools/freigang-messen/' }, { hreflang: 'es', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/es/tools/medir-holgura-coche/' }, { hreflang: 'x-default', href: 'https://atlasgarageos.com/tools/measure-my-car/' }]} eyebrow="User-measured clearance" intro="Capture the two physical gaps Atlas needs to project how a different wheel position changes static clearance." limitation="Measurements represent one observed static condition. Suspension travel, steering angle, alignment, tire shape, load, and body variation remain outside this calculation." studioCta="Start the guided measurement" studioHref="/fitment-studio/#measure-flow">
  <div slot="tool" class="entry-workspace"><div><p class="eyebrow">Measurement checklist</p><h2>Two gaps, tied to one baseline</h2><p>Confirm the wheel and tire currently installed before measuring. Use the shortest relevant static distance on each side.</p><ol class="entry-steps"><li><strong>Inner clearance</strong><span>Wheel or tire area to the nearest fixed suspension or body component.</span></li><li><strong>Outer clearance</strong><span>Outer wheel or tire area to the fender boundary being evaluated.</span></li><li><strong>Optional targets</strong><span>Add only margins you chose; Atlas will not invent one.</span></li></ol></div><a class="button" href="/fitment-studio/#measure-flow">Open the five-step wizard</a></div>
  <div slot="explanation"><h2>Why the baseline matters</h2><p>Clearance measurements are stored with the exact current setup used when they were taken. New wheel positions are projected from that baseline rather than treated as universal vehicle specifications.</p><p>Atlas labels these values USER MEASURED and keeps calculated projections visibly separate.</p></div>
</ToolPage>
